  "description": "<p>Hi,<br/>\nI installed fedora 3.4.2, using mysql database, check install properties.<br/>\nI can create objects fine in <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/fedora/admin\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/fedora/admin</a>, but when I search for objects I get error in flash error msg: Could not retrieve search results due to: Error (404): fedora-system:ContentModel-3.0</p>\n\n<p>ERROR LOGS:</p>\n\n<p>WARN 2011-10-10 17:04:23.127 <span class=\"error\">&#91;http-8080-2&#93;</span> (FedoraObjectSearchResource) Resource not found: fedora-system:ContentModel-3.0; unable to fulfill REST API request<br/>\norg.fcrepo.server.errors.ObjectNotInLowlevelStorageException: fedora-system:ContentModel-3.0<br/>\n        at org.fcrepo.server.storage.lowlevel.akubra.AkubraLowlevelStorage.retrieve(AkubraLowlevelStorage.java:383) <span class=\"error\">&#91;fcrepo-server-3.4.2.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n        at org.fcrepo.server.storage.lowlevel.akubra.AkubraLowlevelStorage.retrieveObject(AkubraLowlevelStorage.java:160) <span class=\"error\">&#91;fcrepo-server-3.4.2.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n        at org.fcrepo.server.storage.lowlevel.akubra.AkubraLowlevelStorageModule.retrieveObject(AkubraLowlevelStorageModule.java:84) <span class=\"error\">&#91;fcrepo-server-3.4.2.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n        at org.fcrepo.server.storage.DefaultDOManager.getReader(DefaultDOManager.java:646) <span class=\"error\">&#91;fcrepo-server-3.4.2.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n        at org.fcrepo.server.search.FieldSearchResultSQLImpl.getObjectFields(FieldSearchResultSQLImpl.java:489) <span class=\"error\">&#91;fcrepo-server-3.4.2.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n        at org.fcrepo.server.search.FieldSearchResultSQLImpl.step(FieldSearchResultSQLImpl.java:401) <span class=\"error\">&#91;fcrepo-server-3.4.2.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n        at org.fcrepo.server.search.FieldSearchSQLImpl.stepAndRemember(FieldSearchSQLImpl.java:352) <span class=\"error\">&#91;fcrepo